{"content":[{"c":["JAAR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Most common word in Hebrew for “forest.” It refers to forests generally (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.10.18","r":"Isa.10.18","rawR":"Isa.10.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.10.18","value":"Isa.10.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 10:18"},") and to specific forests, such as the “forest of Ephraim” (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.18.6","r":"2Sam.18.6","rawR":"2Sam.18.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.18.6","value":"2Sam.18.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 18:6"},") and the “forest of Hereth” (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.5","r":"1Sam.22.5","rawR":"1Sam.22.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.5","value":"1Sam.22.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 22:5"},"), both associated with King David. It also occurs as the name of one of Solomon’s buildings, “the Palace of the Forest of Lebanon” (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.7.2","r":"1Kgs.7.2","rawR":"1Kgs.7.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.7.2","value":"1Kgs.7.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 7:2"},"), apparently because of its extensive use of cedar. Only one occurrence of “Jaar” seems to be a proper name. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.6","r":"Ps.132.6","rawR":"Ps.132.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.6","value":"Ps.132.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 132:6"}," alludes to the transfer of the ark from Kiriath-jearim to Jerusalem. Here it is called the field of Jaar (or “the wood,” ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), perhaps a poetic abbreviation."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Jaar","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Is 10:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.10.18","rawQueryValue":"Isa.10.18","sourceRefExact":"Isa.10.18"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 18:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.18.6","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.18.6","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.18.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 22:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.5","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.5","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.5"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 7:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.7.2","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.7.2","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.7.2"},{"anchorText":"Psalm 132:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.132.6","rawQueryValue":"Ps.132.6","sourceRefExact":"Ps.132.6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"feccb71ba1040bf5c1c22e9aee8daaff477b83c6fa83d28209a0d0a6c3f67ec9","sourceItemName":"Jaar","sourceItemOrder":6,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Jaar","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Jaar","title":"Jaar","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}